WEBVTT

00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:07.530
Shima-chan, I'll take care of that.

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:11.900
But you've already taken on so much, Kouta.

00:00:17.110 --> 00:00:18.910
You won't be able to handle it at this rate.

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:36.890
Sora wo aogi Hoshi yo michite Tobitatsu no Asu e no brilliant road

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:36.890
Look up to the sky, rise to the stars, Take-off on the brilliant road of tomorrow

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:36.890
空を仰ぎ 星よ満ちて 飛び立つの 明日への brilliant road

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:44.840
Kokoro no aosa Kono te ni daite go far away

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:44.840
Carry the unexpierence of the heart in the hands and go far away

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:44.840
心の蒼さ この手に抱いて go far away

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.940
Urayamu koto ni Narete shimattara

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.940
If you have experienced the envy

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.940
羨む事に 慣れてしまったら

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.970
Hokoreru jibun ga Toozakatteku

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.970
Your proud self will go far away

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.970
誇れる自分が 遠ざかってく

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:13.140
Mienai tsubasa de habataku no fly higher

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:13.140
Flapping the invisible wings to fly higher

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:13.140
見えない翼で羽ばたくの fly higher

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:20.470
Yume wo egaku no wa hito ni umareta kara

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:20.470
I'm imaging dreams because I was born a "person"

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:20.470
夢を描くのは「人」に生まれたから

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.580
Sora wo aogi Hoshi yo michite

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.580
Look up to the sky, rise to the stars,

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.580
空を仰ぎ 星よ満ちて

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.040
Tobitatsu no Asu e no brilliant road

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.040
Take-off on the brilliant road of tomorrow.

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.040
飛び立つの 明日への brilliant road

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.920
Kokoro no aosa Kono te ni daite

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.920
Carry the unexperienced of the heart in the hands

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.920
心の蒼さ この手に抱いて

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
Anata to nara Yowai jibun wo sarakedashite hashiridaseru no

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
If I were with you, I'd start running, exposing my weak self

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
あなたとなら 弱い自分をさらけ出して走り出せるの

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
Mirai yo dou ka Mugen ni tsuzuke go far away

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
The future! Somehow continues to the infinity, go far away

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
未来よどうか 無限に続け go far away

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:07.140
Episode Twenty-Two: 
Their Own Path

00:02:14.460 --> 00:02:18.160
Miss Leila, A109's retrieval operations have been completed.

00:02:18.390 --> 00:02:19.230
Good work.

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:21.900
Switch with Kusanagi's group and take a short break.

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:23.160
We can still work.

00:02:23.770 --> 00:02:25.130
It's not good to be greedy.

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:29.090
Let those who couldn't participate in the Great Mission have some work.

00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:32.360
This is a prestigious role, isn't it? I understand.

00:02:34.930 --> 00:02:37.010
Going as far as mobilizing the students...

00:02:37.710 --> 00:02:39.500
This is tougher than the Great Mission...

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:41.610
...because we don't have time to prepare.

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:57.430
Welcome to space.

00:02:58.120 --> 00:03:01.840
I'm Jinrai Shirogane, commander of the Stellvia's forces.

00:03:02.430 --> 00:03:03.560
I'm Lecio Suljette...

00:03:03.590 --> 00:03:06.310
...the high commissioner for the Sol System Federation.

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:08.620
You're a young commander.

00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:10.950
That means you were chosen from a very select few, doesn't it?

00:03:11.390 --> 00:03:14.320
I was chosen due to the actual battle experience I gained at the Ultima.

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:16.290
That's valuable experience.

00:03:16.950 --> 00:03:18.390
After all, there aren't many...

00:03:18.910 --> 00:03:21.150
...who've experienced battle these past 180 years.

00:03:21.690 --> 00:03:22.820
We're counting on you.

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:25.890
The plan for the firing system that centers around the Infinity...

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:27.730
...has been completed.

00:03:28.280 --> 00:03:33.750
Only, the conditions for the Fracture's lowest energy point haven't been met.

00:03:34.820 --> 00:03:37.840
It looks like Professor Turner will be sending the equipment...

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:40.410
...that was developed on the Akapusu, but...

00:03:41.030 --> 00:03:45.320
That will help us, but the problem isn't the hardware. It's the software.

00:03:45.810 --> 00:03:48.730
We need an advanced mathematical model...

00:03:49.070 --> 00:03:51.700
...that can analyze the Fracture's complex energy shifts.

00:03:52.050 --> 00:03:54.820
What is our chance of success at this point?

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:57.900
0.73%.

00:03:58.500 --> 00:03:59.510
What did you say?

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:01.710
That is the highest percentage...

00:04:02.350 --> 00:04:05.730
The chance of humanity surviving is 0.73 percent...

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:10.180
Of course, we will announce a higher percentage to the rest of the world.

00:04:13.570 --> 00:04:18.020
There are now 38 days until Genesis Mission begins.

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:22.960
According to simulations, damage to the Earth will be insignificant...

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:23.490
And we thought the Great Mission was finally over, too...

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:25.880
...so all citizens are asked to please be orderly in their reactions...

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:27.390
It's all right, isn't it? After all, thanks to this, school is closed.

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:31.560
Easygoing, aren't you? We're helping with the loading work, too.

00:04:32.650 --> 00:04:35.260
And the damage the Fracture will cause is...

00:04:35.510 --> 00:04:36.770
Won't it be all right?

00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:40.300
The news said there wouldn't be much of an effect on the Earth, after all...

00:04:40.490 --> 00:04:42.900
The Earth will be fine, but what about the Foundations?

00:04:43.180 --> 00:04:44.560
Oh... right.

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:46.390
There! That's the vital point right there!

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:47.980
I'm telling you it'll be all right.

00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:50.720
Kouta and Shipon will deal with it well.

00:04:51.620 --> 00:04:53.180
And my papa is here, too.

00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:16.950
Would it be possible to make it so I could use Infi's DLS by myself?

00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:19.800
Are you worried about Miss Katase?

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:24.040
I asked because I thought it would be more efficient to manage it by myself.

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:28.350
Well, just as you say, it would be more efficient to design it...

00:05:28.630 --> 00:05:30.450
...so that it was all configured for you.

00:05:30.980 --> 00:05:32.020
But...

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:34.650
It appears Miss Katase is too insecure.

00:05:34.990 --> 00:05:37.390
I think this is a proposal that merits investigation...

00:05:37.890 --> 00:05:38.750
I am against it.

00:05:39.740 --> 00:05:42.020
She has potential.

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:43.800
Potential, you say?

00:05:44.130 --> 00:05:46.310
You're going to make Shima-chan do this because of something so vague?

00:05:46.710 --> 00:05:51.100
It makes sense that the world is vague, Kouta Otoyama.

00:05:52.170 --> 00:05:54.310
There is nothing definite.

00:05:54.630 --> 00:05:55.110
But...

00:05:55.640 --> 00:05:59.110
To say nothing else, this new technology, the DLS...

00:05:59.490 --> 00:06:01.680
...and human beings, both have insecure existences.

00:06:02.210 --> 00:06:05.880
But because they are vague, you can gain something from them.

00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:14.930
Shipon, we're ready.

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:18.140
Okay. I'll be right there.

00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:27.370
Rinna will be handling navigation, Shipon will be handling power output.

00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:29.850
It's an instant Infi.

00:06:30.140 --> 00:06:33.720
This will be practice for how to follow through for your partner.

00:06:34.010 --> 00:06:35.320
It was Shipon's idea.

00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:38.060
I'm the one who made it a two-seater.

00:06:38.150 --> 00:06:39.510
Is this all right?

00:06:38.760 --> 00:06:41.290
She's been trying too hard recently, hasn't she?

00:06:39.510 --> 00:06:41.470
Yeah. Fly as fast as you want.

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:45.270
Now Shipon thinks she's a burden on Kouta.

00:06:45.490 --> 00:06:47.300
Shipon's doing all right.

00:06:47.780 --> 00:06:50.300
But she doesn't think so.

00:06:50.990 --> 00:06:53.740
Whether they make up or break up, she can't face Kouta...

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:58.940
...until she gets rid of that feeling of being a burden.

00:06:59.370 --> 00:07:01.540
I see... You're right.

00:07:02.240 --> 00:07:03.250
It's all right!

00:07:03.800 --> 00:07:06.790
Rinna, it's all right to use irregular maneuvers, too.

00:07:07.180 --> 00:07:08.140
Will you be able to keep up?

00:07:08.370 --> 00:07:09.750
Yeah, I'll be fine.

00:07:10.010 --> 00:07:12.260
All right! Here I go!

00:07:15.250 --> 00:07:18.890
If I can't cope with this much, then I won't be able to catch up with Kouta.

00:07:28.430 --> 00:07:30.080
Still too soon... is it?

00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:32.250
Mr. Hutter.
 Hmm?

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:41.420
Commissioner Suljett is waiting.

00:07:41.970 --> 00:07:44.430
Could you please come to the main room?

00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:47.320
Is something the matter?

00:07:47.610 --> 00:07:49.590
I will be... a little late.

00:07:49.980 --> 00:07:51.830
What? 
I have to make a side stop.

00:07:57.470 --> 00:07:58.100
By yourself?

00:07:59.750 --> 00:08:01.660
You can tell without having to ask, can't you?

00:08:02.120 --> 00:08:03.110
I'm all by myself.

00:08:03.570 --> 00:08:05.130
I wanted to make you say it.

00:08:05.680 --> 00:08:06.440
Mean, wasn't it?

00:08:07.650 --> 00:08:09.840
Is it all right to leave your partner be?

00:08:10.310 --> 00:08:12.710
When we're together, it's hard on both of us.

00:08:13.050 --> 00:08:14.150
That's not...

00:08:14.670 --> 00:08:18.550
I don't want to hurt her anymore. That's why...

00:08:19.850 --> 00:08:22.510
I do want her to be by my side.

00:08:23.690 --> 00:08:25.200
It's lonely being by myself.

00:08:25.720 --> 00:08:28.610
Even though I never thought that way until now.

00:08:29.480 --> 00:08:30.950
But... now...

00:08:35.640 --> 00:08:38.150
Then I'll stay with you until you finish drinking.

00:08:39.190 --> 00:08:43.010
In exchange, you're going to go to Miss Katase when you finish.

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:48.130
Okay, sempai.

00:08:52.520 --> 00:08:53.680
We need to go soon...

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:56.020
It's our turn to guide, right?

00:08:56.200 --> 00:08:57.850
Hey, Shipon!

00:08:58.250 --> 00:09:00.560
We have to go now.

00:09:01.290 --> 00:09:05.130
You've already done seven sets of ten. You should take a break.

00:09:05.620 --> 00:09:08.800
I see, we've worked that hard.

00:09:09.350 --> 00:09:10.400
Let's take a break, Shipon.

00:09:10.860 --> 00:09:14.010
Okay, but just a little more.

00:09:14.390 --> 00:09:18.520
You were onboard Infi before you started practicing with us, right?

00:09:18.950 --> 00:09:22.400
Being sure to take a break is an important job for a pilot, too.

00:09:22.970 --> 00:09:26.210
That's right. It's not good to strain yourself too much.

00:09:26.590 --> 00:09:31.130
Thanks. But I'll definitely take a break after one more.

00:09:31.360 --> 00:09:32.080
Rest!
 Rest!

00:09:32.260 --> 00:09:33.260
R-Right!

00:09:33.790 --> 00:09:34.730
Yeesh...

00:09:35.260 --> 00:09:38.700
She seems all spaced out, but Shipon is actually stubborn.

00:09:40.790 --> 00:09:42.710
And you're in really good spirits.

00:09:42.900 --> 00:09:44.570
This is still just the beginning.

00:09:47.990 --> 00:09:51.830
Input Rinna's linked data, and set it to random...

00:09:52.670 --> 00:09:54.000
I'm sorry, everyone.

00:09:54.640 --> 00:09:56.750
I'll rest after I work for a little bit more...

00:10:03.690 --> 00:10:07.520
Well, I had an objection to the students being mobilized, but...

00:10:08.170 --> 00:10:10.370
...they know space well.

00:10:10.740 --> 00:10:13.170
They have more experience than the adults that are on Earth, so...

00:10:15.430 --> 00:10:17.110
You're the team from the Vision, right?

00:10:17.600 --> 00:10:19.950
Please head to Hangar Number One.

00:10:20.520 --> 00:10:22.460
Please move starting with the groups that are finished.

00:10:22.740 --> 00:10:25.520
After this, we're going to begin the work to construct the generators.

00:10:26.240 --> 00:10:27.230
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:10:27.370 --> 00:10:29.280
Good work. We're here to relieve you!

00:10:30.490 --> 00:10:34.630
Be careful. The B4 block has been changed to the Akapusu team.

00:10:34.830 --> 00:10:35.440
Thanks.

00:10:35.870 --> 00:10:38.970
Hey, you came for us, my honey.

00:10:39.280 --> 00:10:40.660
I wonder if I should fire...

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:42.520
O-Oh, you kidder, Yayoi...

00:10:43.130 --> 00:10:45.140
There's no gun attached, after all...

00:10:49.380 --> 00:10:50.010
What in the world?

00:11:12.450 --> 00:11:15.400
"Would it be possible to make it so I could use the DLS by myself?"

00:11:16.120 --> 00:11:17.900
Kouta Otoyama came to us and asked this.

00:11:18.940 --> 00:11:20.930
I... see.

00:11:21.470 --> 00:11:22.400
The Direct Link System...

00:11:22.950 --> 00:11:27.170
...is still a system that chooses the people that can pilot it.

00:11:27.980 --> 00:11:31.010
Your skills as a pilot and as a programmer...

00:11:31.570 --> 00:11:33.680
...as well as your strength of will, are desirable.

00:11:34.570 --> 00:11:38.510
At its current level, it's normal for humanity to not be able to handle it.

00:11:40.270 --> 00:11:43.460
How about leaving Infinity to him?

00:11:45.160 --> 00:11:47.150
Kouta Otoyama is special.

00:11:48.310 --> 00:11:50.450
He's not someone you will be able to catch up to.

00:11:51.060 --> 00:11:54.210
That might be true. That might be true, but...

00:11:57.760 --> 00:12:00.690
What is your reason for trying so hard?

00:12:01.700 --> 00:12:04.100
Is it because you have a sense of duty to save mankind?

00:12:04.790 --> 00:12:06.280
Are you matching your willpower against his?

00:12:06.560 --> 00:12:08.930
Is it love for him? Or could it be...

00:12:09.500 --> 00:12:10.050
I...

00:12:11.180 --> 00:12:15.200
When I looked up at space from the Earth, that's when I thought it.

00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:18.150
That I didn't want to just look up.

00:12:18.930 --> 00:12:20.490
That's why I came to space.

00:12:21.530 --> 00:12:22.890
I feel the same about Kouta.

00:12:23.470 --> 00:12:25.610
I don't want to just look at him from far away.

00:12:26.250 --> 00:12:28.880
I want to be with Kouta.

00:12:29.400 --> 00:12:31.800
I want to see what he sees along with him.

00:12:32.350 --> 00:12:35.120
I want to be onboard the Infi that Kouta's onboard, too.

00:12:36.020 --> 00:12:38.410
I don't know if I'll reach him or not...

00:12:38.680 --> 00:12:41.150
...but I want to get closer to him, even if just a little bit.

00:12:41.600 --> 00:12:42.250
That's why...

00:12:43.540 --> 00:12:48.050
Um... they say the journey of 1,000 miles begins with one step, right?

00:12:48.570 --> 00:12:51.610
I don't want to give up on walking.

00:12:52.100 --> 00:12:53.860
The journey of 1,000 miles begins with one step.

00:12:54.560 --> 00:12:56.320
Rome wasn't built in a day...

00:12:57.940 --> 00:13:01.240
A large urietta is a gathering of small alesa.

00:13:02.340 --> 00:13:02.910
Hmm?

00:13:06.040 --> 00:13:07.840
The emergency call sign...

00:13:08.490 --> 00:13:10.580
Take off, starting with the Katies that have clearance!

00:13:11.420 --> 00:13:14.100
Work groups that are finished, return to the Stellvia at once.

00:13:14.800 --> 00:13:16.490
All Biancas, begin recovery detail!

00:13:18.730 --> 00:13:20.290
Of all things, at a time like this...

00:13:20.670 --> 00:13:25.700
"Despair is the sickness unto death," said Kierkegaard.

00:13:26.050 --> 00:13:29.310
Exactly! If we don't give up, then it will work out somehow.

00:13:36.230 --> 00:13:37.930
What the...? What are they?

00:13:38.680 --> 00:13:39.780
I know...

00:13:40.790 --> 00:13:41.890
I know what they are!

00:13:43.250 --> 00:13:44.290
Rinna! 
Rinna!

00:13:45.970 --> 00:13:49.010
Stop it, Kazamatsuri! The Biancas are on recovery detail!

00:13:49.610 --> 00:13:52.300
They destroyed our Ultima!

00:13:52.800 --> 00:13:55.140
I know. I was there, too.

00:13:55.220 --> 00:13:56.030
In that case!

00:13:58.460 --> 00:13:59.190
Rinna!

00:13:59.420 --> 00:14:00.690
Yayoi, get out of the way!

00:14:01.120 --> 00:14:02.800
Calm down, Rinna!

00:14:03.180 --> 00:14:05.670
You don't understand, which is why you can say that, Yayoi!

00:14:05.950 --> 00:14:08.550
I saw them, the people covered in blood.

00:14:08.530 --> 00:14:09.080
Listen!

00:14:09.360 --> 00:14:12.340
I wasn't able to launch at that time. That's why...

00:14:12.570 --> 00:14:13.210
Listen!

00:14:14.220 --> 00:14:17.980
Trust the commander's instructions. He was... there too.

00:14:19.890 --> 00:14:21.970
All Katies are to stand by in your designated positions.

00:14:22.640 --> 00:14:24.220
No one on our side is to lay a finger on them, no matter what!

00:14:24.920 --> 00:14:26.770
All workers, hurry up on the evacuation!

00:14:26.970 --> 00:14:28.250
We should attack them.

00:14:29.920 --> 00:14:32.530
Our opponents have ignored our warnings...

00:14:32.640 --> 00:14:34.640
...and are clearly violating our airspace.

00:14:34.870 --> 00:14:38.370
That's our rule. Their rules are...

00:14:38.370 --> 00:14:40.160
If we were attacked by the enemy now...

00:14:40.620 --> 00:14:42.850
...what would happen to the generator assembly work?

00:14:43.630 --> 00:14:45.390
Have you forgotten what happened to the Ultima?

00:14:45.910 --> 00:14:47.620
I will not give the order to attack!

00:14:48.290 --> 00:14:50.690
Can you take responsibility for humanity's future?

00:14:51.090 --> 00:14:52.420
I will try!

00:14:54.680 --> 00:14:57.540
Mr. Hutter, thank you very much!

00:14:58.200 --> 00:15:00.520
A small alesa. But...

00:15:06.790 --> 00:15:07.830
Please come to a halt.

00:15:08.470 --> 00:15:10.870
If you approach any further, it will be seen as a hostile action.

00:15:11.970 --> 00:15:14.270
I repeat, please come to a halt!

00:15:17.750 --> 00:15:21.140
A wave that we believe is a transmission is being sent to us.

00:15:21.630 --> 00:15:24.050
Link the analysis program to the DLS.

00:15:24.350 --> 00:15:28.100
All units that have stopped their work, back up the Infinity!

00:15:28.390 --> 00:15:28.880
- Yes, sir! - Yes, sir!

00:15:29.750 --> 00:15:31.460
We have to read their intentions.

00:15:33.280 --> 00:15:34.520
A preemptive attack!

00:15:35.070 --> 00:15:38.660
It's your responsibility to protect the Genesis Mission's equipment, isn't it?

00:15:38.950 --> 00:15:43.170
No. It's my responsibility to protect humanity's future!

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:49.470
Commander Orihara. As his superior, you give the order to attack.

00:15:49.990 --> 00:15:52.480
He is too young to be burdened with the future of the Earth.

00:15:52.940 --> 00:15:55.520
It's because he's young that I want him to have the burden.

00:15:56.930 --> 00:15:58.500
Mr. Shirogane, I believe in you...

00:15:58.500 --> 00:16:00.980
...you who personally experienced what happened at the Ultima.

00:16:01.240 --> 00:16:03.500
But if these decisions are too heavy a burden...

00:16:03.820 --> 00:16:04.370
No, sir.

00:16:04.970 --> 00:16:05.700
It's all right.

00:16:08.180 --> 00:16:09.730
All personnel, maintain present conditions!

00:16:10.380 --> 00:16:11.650
They are not the enemy!

00:16:13.160 --> 00:16:16.200
You guys head back! I can handle this by myself.

00:16:16.630 --> 00:16:17.230
But...

00:16:17.640 --> 00:16:18.420
Infi is coming!

00:16:18.710 --> 00:16:20.200
Otoyama, Miss Katase!

00:16:20.590 --> 00:16:21.200
Shipon?!

00:16:28.600 --> 00:16:29.640
Shipon...

00:16:30.710 --> 00:16:32.150
Shima-chan, there's not going to be any fighting.

00:16:32.420 --> 00:16:36.550
Right. We're going to decipher their transmissions, right?

00:16:37.390 --> 00:16:39.950
We're going to use the system right up to the limit. Can you do it?

00:16:40.340 --> 00:16:41.840
I'll do my best!

00:16:43.580 --> 00:16:46.580
This is the transmission protocol that we use.

00:16:47.710 --> 00:16:48.580
We...

00:16:50.860 --> 00:16:55.320
In other words, we'll understand their transmissions' contents using that?

00:16:57.110 --> 00:16:58.380
Is that all right?

00:16:59.080 --> 00:17:03.440
Isn't it against your rules to help us?

00:17:04.250 --> 00:17:08.530
I have observed the planet called Earth for 800 days.

00:17:10.410 --> 00:17:12.230
Earthlings are still young.

00:17:13.270 --> 00:17:14.660
They are passionate, straightforward...

00:17:15.730 --> 00:17:18.280
...and they still don't understand themselves.

00:17:19.550 --> 00:17:21.830
If we made casual contact with them in this state...

00:17:22.060 --> 00:17:24.730
...it would be certain to cause chaos and conflict.

00:17:25.510 --> 00:17:27.360
Not counting the instance with the Ultima...

00:17:28.280 --> 00:17:30.970
That is why I maintained a distance.

00:17:31.900 --> 00:17:33.660
That is the proper choice, right?

00:17:34.850 --> 00:17:35.740
But...

00:17:38.370 --> 00:17:41.150
Nothing changes when all you do is look at it from far away.

00:17:41.870 --> 00:17:45.990
Even if you try to backtrack in time step by step...

00:17:46.560 --> 00:17:47.660
...if you don't step forward...

00:17:49.650 --> 00:17:52.830
A large urietta is a gathering of small alesa.

00:17:53.010 --> 00:17:53.410
Hmm?

00:17:54.340 --> 00:17:56.040
It's a saying on my planet.

00:17:56.680 --> 00:18:02.040
Thank you. It makes me very happy that you feel that way.

00:18:02.690 --> 00:18:05.990
It is you Earthlings that made me feel that way.

00:18:07.960 --> 00:18:10.360
Well then, shall we go? 
Hmm?

00:18:11.220 --> 00:18:13.830
We have to watch over our students.

00:18:15.130 --> 00:18:17.380
Open up channel C-7.

00:18:18.220 --> 00:18:20.970
We're going to send you a transmission protocol now.

00:18:21.550 --> 00:18:23.090
A transmission protocol?

00:18:23.740 --> 00:18:27.710
If you use it, you should be able to decipher their transmissions.

00:18:28.600 --> 00:18:30.340
When did you get something like that?

00:18:30.940 --> 00:18:32.270
It's something you can trust.

00:18:33.520 --> 00:18:35.280
Miss Shima Katase. 
 Yes, sir?

00:18:35.830 --> 00:18:36.990
The journey of 1,000 miles...

00:18:39.420 --> 00:18:40.200
Begins with one step!

00:18:44.220 --> 00:18:44.650
Here we go.

00:18:48.660 --> 00:18:49.910
Please, Shipon.

00:18:50.380 --> 00:18:52.290
I don't want what happened to the Ultima to happen anymore.

00:18:55.230 --> 00:18:58.990
Infi's synchronization complete. Fix the port at number eight.

00:19:08.190 --> 00:19:08.910
It's not disappearing...

00:19:11.920 --> 00:19:13.310
That can't be...

00:19:18.740 --> 00:19:21.190
I don't understand... I can't see anything...

00:19:29.700 --> 00:19:31.350
Kouta, sorry to keep you waiting.

00:19:32.200 --> 00:19:33.000
Shima-chan!

00:19:33.640 --> 00:19:35.050
There's still quite a bit left, isn't there?

00:19:35.720 --> 00:19:38.750
It looks like I really did leave too much to you, Kouta.

00:19:39.100 --> 00:19:40.780
You're finished with your part, Shima-chan?

00:19:41.390 --> 00:19:43.670
If you do it little by little, it goes pretty fast.

00:19:43.990 --> 00:19:45.580
R-Right...

00:19:49.160 --> 00:19:53.950
If method A doesn't work, then B might.

00:19:54.250 --> 00:19:55.090
I see.

00:19:55.470 --> 00:19:59.850
You mean Shima Katase and Kouta Otoyama have different potentials.

00:20:00.700 --> 00:20:02.700
This isn't limited to the two of them.

00:20:03.190 --> 00:20:07.640
Isn't it for this reason that humans exist as a group...

00:20:08.020 --> 00:20:09.780
...that possess varied genotypes?

00:20:13.190 --> 00:20:14.000
Operation complete!

00:20:14.440 --> 00:20:16.870
Transmitting the results of the analysis to the Stellvia.

00:20:18.510 --> 00:20:19.240
It's arrived!

00:20:21.440 --> 00:20:23.260
It's a map of the Cosmic Fracture.

00:20:23.400 --> 00:20:25.190
Technical Officer Kazamatsuri, with this...

00:20:26.520 --> 00:20:27.480
Yes, it'll work.

00:20:28.230 --> 00:20:30.690
The Genesis Mission will work!

00:20:36.500 --> 00:20:37.110
They vanished?

00:20:37.630 --> 00:20:41.210
Shipon drove them off! Yay!

00:20:41.270 --> 00:20:42.340
Yay!

00:20:42.570 --> 00:20:43.730
The danger has gone away!

00:20:44.280 --> 00:20:45.150
All right!

00:20:45.670 --> 00:20:47.030
You did it, Shipon!

00:20:50.530 --> 00:20:53.070
I wonder if they've made up a little.

00:20:56.570 --> 00:20:57.320
It's over.

00:21:01.400 --> 00:21:03.100
You made a wise decision.

00:21:07.760 --> 00:21:08.800
Thank you very much.

00:21:09.640 --> 00:21:11.980
I am going to recommend to the Federation...

00:21:12.240 --> 00:21:15.620
...that you be the commander of the Genesis Mission.

00:21:27.450 --> 00:21:29.420
Does that mean they're finished with their business here?

00:21:29.480 --> 00:21:30.310
It looks like it.

00:21:35.720 --> 00:21:38.790
Shima-chan... um... About earlier...

00:21:39.160 --> 00:21:40.060
Earlier?

00:21:41.360 --> 00:21:42.110
Thanks...

00:21:44.020 --> 00:21:44.480
Sure...

00:21:46.450 --> 00:21:48.210
I'm looking forward to working with you from here on, too...

00:21:51.310 --> 00:21:52.410
Same here.

00:21:55.960 --> 00:22:01.050
kono sora no iku hate ni

